  "importantNotes": [
    "A pronoun's case is determined by its grammatical job, not simply by its position in the sentence.",
    "English 'it' follows the gender of the German noun: der becomes er, die becomes sie, and das becomes es.",
    "In the dative plural, many nouns also receive an additional -n, as in 'mit diesen Leuten'."
  ],
